{"question": "What happens after the FSO takes a sample?",
 "answer": "When the FSO takes a sample:\n\n1. He submits it to the lab\n2. The lab performs the analysis and provides a result\n3. If the result is OK, then no action is taken\n4. If the result is not OK, the FBO will face a penalty\n5. After a non-satisfactory result, the FBO can appeal to the designated officer in Form VIII",
 "intent": "procedure",
 "documents": ["workflow"],
 "query_type": "procedure",
 "evidence": "The Sampling section (## Sampling) describes the full procedure from submission through appeal."}

